2627202](https://github.com/Parikshit-Sahrawat/OpsControl_Dashboard/actions/runs/42532627202) — in_progress at trigger snapshot; result PENDING.\n- [OC Dev - Tier A - UAT Controller Safety Contracts - No Deploy — 42532627092](https://github.com/Parikshit-Sahrawat/OpsControl_Dashboard/actions/runs/42532627092) — in_progress at trigger snapshot; result PENDING.\n- [OC Dev - Tier B - Operational Dashboard Integration — 42532627212](https://github.com/Parikshit-Sahrawat/OpsControl_Dashboard/actions/runs/42532627212) — in_progress at trigger snapshot; result PENDING.\n- [OC Dev - Tier C - Application Image and Worker Validation - No Deploy — 42532627312](https://github.com/Parikshit-Sahrawat/OpsControl_Dashboard/actions/runs/42532627312) — in_progress at trigger snapshot; result PENDING.\n\n### Explicit remaining blockers\n\n- All13 existing required checks are preserved. No ruleset/check removal or weakening. Prior Administration-write403 remains a prerequisite for any future authorized equivalent-check transition.\n- Seven-role final image builds/scans pending hosted evidence; local Docker backing storage observed0 free. Official patched Python/nginx/PostgreSQL candidate recipes prepared. Fresh **base-only** registry scans remain failures: nginx1 Critical; PostgreSQL4 Critical/32 High. These are not final application deltas or clearance.\n- OTel0.123.0 immutable binary/pin is unchanged and retains compiled-in findings, including in UAT. Supported transition/compatibility approval is required; no unapproved fork or binary upgrade. Debian vendor-wont-fix findings and licence/NOTICE/source-offer signoff remain unresolved.\n- Coordinated child API-source environment cutover still fails closed409; multi-source revision UI/command work remains. Catalogue publication CAS and provider-specific applicability/qualification remain separate gaps. Drafts are browser-memory only.\n- **Owner visual acceptance and independent engineering PR review requested**. Newly tested functionality is not owner acceptance, formal UAT, genuine-provider certification, release approval or permission to merge.\n- No merge, deployment, publication, collector upgrade, security waiver or Sprint2 work. Nine owner selections/D07/D08 remain pending.\n\n**CHK-001 FAIL · CHK-002 BLOCKED · SECURITY BLOCKED · RELEASE NO-GO.**\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prior PR description and evidence handoff (historical)</summary>\n\n## Consolidated implementation handoff — 2026-11-08\n\nFinal HEAD: `4081fc75117afbd43e1fc4489925a2d65d744551`. Main baseline: `2e4fe5d8cb0f39170b0d789fdd7e07be4ac0219a`. PR remains **draft; PARTIAL/BLOCKED; Sprint 1 NOT COMPLETE**.\n\nAll six pinned source heads (#80, #81, #82, #83, #84, #86) are ancestors through proper three-way merges; main already contains #85. Source branches and main were not modified. Semantic conflicts preserve ETL, ownership/RBAC, migration guards, policy, workspace/theme and Incidents UI retirement.\n\n### Changes and evidence\n\n- Additive migration 0042, immutable tenant-scoped source revision ledger, actor/time/hash/provenance, source expected-revision/idempotency commands and transactional legacy attachment adapters.\n- Typed host OS/method and explicit HTTPS applicability; unverified/incompatible/excluded configurations fail closed. New-revision rollback revalidates and never activates collectors or restores secrets/checkpoints.\n- Approved single-panel three-level navigation, tenant/session reload safeguards, actual API/browser configuration tests and desktop captures.\n- Preserve all 28 workflows and 13 required checks; no retired coverage. Source configuration acceptance and tamper-resistant evidence checks added.\n- [Report and commands](https://github.com/Parikshit-Sahrawat/OpsControl_Dashboard/tree/4081fc75117afbd43e1fc4489925a2d65d744551/docs/verification/sprint1-integration/REPORT.md), [merge decisions](https://github.com/Parikshit-Sahrawat/OpsControl_Dashboard/tree/4081fc75117afbd43e1fc4489925a2d65d744551/docs/verification/sprint1-integration/MERGE_RESOLUTIONS.md), [changed files](https://github.com/Parikshit-Sahrawat/OpsControl_Dashboard/tree/4081fc75117afbd43e1fc4489925a2d65d744551/docs/verification/sprint1-integration/CONSOLIDATED_CHANGED_FILES.txt), [source identities](https://github.com/Parikshit-Sahrawat/OpsControl_Dashboard/tree/4081fc75117afbd43e1fc4489925a2d65d744551/docs/verification/sprint1-integration/TESTED_SOURCE_SHA256.json).\n- [1,273 artifact checksums](https://github.com/Parikshit-Sahrawat/OpsControl_Dashboard/tree/4081fc75117afbd43e1fc4489925a2d65d744551/docs/verification/sprint1-integration/ARTIFACT_SHA256.json), manifest SHA-256 `37c06b2fda5a6e8fc67fde957334a80c0badee2f121947b430b0209c503ccc88`.\n\n### Actual local results — overlapping suites, not additive\n\n| Suite | Result |\n|---|---|\n|Broad PostgreSQL discovery|662 executions: 594 PASS, 0 FAIL, 68 SKIPPED|\n|Owned ETL PostgreSQL/HTTP/browser|117 PASS, 0 FAIL/SKIP|\n|Final source configuration/ETL subset|38 PASS, 0 FAIL/SKIP|\n|Frontend|55 PASS; lint and production build PASS|\n|CI regression and workflow validation|24 PASS; all 28 workflows valid|\n|Full controlled HTTP/browser/restore/TLS|13 top-level groups PASS; 67 scope HTTP checks, 17 scope-browser groups, 7 closure-browser groups|\n|Operational/theme|PASS; 13 theme checks, 6 contrast measurements, no page/server errors|\n|Historical image policy|7 roles FAIL; unresolved vulnerabilities and pending licence review|\n\n642 unique backend unittest identities have PASS execution evidence after deduplication; 68 discovery skips remain skips and have separate owned execution evidence. Full suites tested 89f8a55; operational/release harness 76c53e9; final product follow-up 917da63; CI implementation 25cd3bf. Exact per-suite SHAs, failed attempts, raw logs, restore comparisons and scoped cleanup are retained. Documentation-only final commits do not relabel older hosted runs as final passes.\n\n### CI TRIGGERED — RESULT PENDING\n\nOne trigger snapshot only;